{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42347 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Stepharine is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in epigenetic regulation. The evidence suggests that Stepharine acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Pelargonidin 3-O-glucoside and 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, which are themselves targets of the compound 7,10-Epoxycyclodeca(b)furan-2(4H)-one, a complex natural product. These compounds are likely to modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in gene silencing. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Stepharine may influence epigenetic processes, possibly through the modulation of DNA polymerase eta, which is a critical enzyme in DNA replication and repair. The evidence supports a role for Stepharine in the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a possible link between Stepharine and epigenetic control mechanisms.",
